  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Today Teacher Kim has a computer lesson. Ben goes to the classroom. May is at the door. \"Hi, May!\" says Ben. \"Hello, Ben!\" says May. Leo comes to the door too. \"Good morning, Leo,\" says May. \"Hello, hello!\" says Leo. Teacher Kim says, \"Good morning, class!\" \"Good morning, Teacher Kim!\" say the children.",
      "The children sit at the computers. \"Today we learn the keyboard,\" says Teacher Kim. \"Please find hello on the computer.\" Ben writes hello. May writes hi. Leo hits the keyboard. The computer says hello, hello, hello! \"Sorry, Teacher Kim!\" says Leo. \"Don't worry, Leo,\" says Teacher Kim. The children smile.",
      "Now it is the end of class. \"Bye, Teacher Kim!\" says May. \"Goodbye, May!\" says Teacher Kim. \"See you, Ben!\" says Leo. \"See you, Leo!\" says Ben. \"Thank you, Teacher Kim,\" says Leo. Teacher Kim smiles. \"Bye, children!\" The children learn hello and bye. Do you say bye to your teacher?"
    ],
    "summary": "Ben, May, and Leo greet each other at the door of the computer classroom. They write greetings on the keyboard, and then they say bye.",
